WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.380
All-seeing evil eyes, teddy bears bent on
murder, and of course, the end of the world.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.896
But which billion-dollar movie was the best?

00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:12.240
The fourth film in the "Transformers" franchise,
"Age of Extinction" added Hollywood star Mark

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.350
Wahlberg, which helped reinvigorate the series.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.760
In the film, a new villain emerges called
Lockdown, a Transformer bounty hunter who

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.820
has come to Earth to kill Optimus Prime.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.640
Unfortunately, the film quickly devolves confusing
large-scale battle scenes and a mess of mind-numbing

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.890
CGI — which, to be fair, is kind of the
whole "Transformers" style.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:34.069
Fans burnt out by "Age of Extinction's" excesses
failed to turn up for the sequel, effectively

00:00:34.069 --> 00:00:35.558
ending the franchise.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.429
Released in 2011, "Dark of the Moon" is the
final "Transformers" film to feature original

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:42.469
series star Shia LeBeouf.

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:46.760
In the film, it's revealed that the original
Apollo mission to the moon in 1969 was actually

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.269
a covert reconnaissance mission that uncovered
a massive Cybertronian starship.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:55.350
The robot inside ends up betraying the Autobots,
threatening to tip the balance of power in

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.030
their cosmic war.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.289
Once again, Michael Bay worked his magic assembling
a surprisingly high caliber supporting cast

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:04.089
of stars, including John Malkovich, and Frances
McDormand.

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:09.750
Heck, there was even an appearance from actual
Apollo 11 astronaut and national hero Buzz Aldrin!

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.610
"From a fellow space traveler, it's a true
honor."

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:15.330
"The honor is mine."

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.790
But ultimately the film was let down by an
overwrought story and over-the-top spectacle

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.882
that bludgeons rather than delights.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:27.660
Loosely inspired by a mostly unrelated novel
also named "On Stranger Tides," the fourth

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.050
"Pirates of the Caribbean" film sees Captain
Jack Sparrow reunite with a former flame who

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.940
delivers Sparrow into the clutches of the
dreaded Blackbeard.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:40.000
The mission: locate the fabled fountain of
youth with a ship full of zombified pirates.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.090
Despite a promising premise, though, the movie
doesn't live up to the chills and thrills

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.300
of earlier entries in the series.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.170
It received poor reviews from fans and critics
alike, causing the sequel, "Dead Men Tell

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:54.050
No Tales" to sink on arrival, ending the Jack
Sparrow saga as we know it… despite his

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.880
master plan to save it.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:00.340
"We shall need a crossbow, an hourglass, three
goats, one of us must learn to play the trumpet

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.255
whilst the other one goes like this!"

00:02:02.385 --> 00:02:06.320
To its credit, "Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom"
attempts to do something different than its

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.870
predecessor, "Jurassic World."

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:12.129
After the island goes awry, our heroes gather
the dinosaurs and move them to a new sanctuary

00:02:12.129 --> 00:02:17.030
at Lockwood Manor, residence of Jurassic Park's
original secretive co-founder Benjamin Lockwood.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.400
But it turns out that Lockwood's minions have
other, more sinister plans for the dinosaurs.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.470
Disjointed and disappointing, it coasted on
its big, bold action scenes and the love audiences

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.849
still had for the "Jurassic Park" franchise.

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:32.269
But critics and audiences alike were unimpressed,
feeling the film lacked the thrills and chills

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:34.003
of the movies that came before it.

00:02:34.248 --> 00:02:38.859
Set decades before the original "Star Wars"
trilogy, "Star Wars: Episode I - The Phantom

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:43.910
Menace" follows veteran Jedi Knight Qui-Gon
Jinn and his protégé Obi-Wan Kenobi as they

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:48.409
uncover a conspiracy on the far-off planet
Naboo, which sets in motion a terrible chain

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:52.239
of events that viewers knew would ultimately
lead to the rise of the evil Empire.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:56.939
"The Phantom Menace" expanded the galaxy with
new additions like Liam Neeson, Ewan McGregor,

00:02:56.939 --> 00:02:59.870
and Natalie Portman, and some cool action
scenes.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:03.730
Unfortunately, that couldn't save the film
from stiff dialogue and backlash on characters

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:04.730
like Jar-Jar Binks.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.019
"Monsters out there, leaking in here, all
sinking and no power?

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:12.882
When are you thinking we're in trouble?!”

00:03:13.156 --> 00:03:18.529
The first in a new wave of Disney live action
remakes, the 2010 big budget blockbuster "Alice

00:03:18.529 --> 00:03:22.610
in Wonderland" was led by celebrated director
Tim Burton, who assembled a cast of stars

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:26.019
to bring his mad retelling of the classic
children's story to life.

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:29.610
The film wasn't without its critics, who in
particular called out its generic climax.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:34.590
But with its talented cast, outrageous style,
and eccentric visuals, audiences largely embraced

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:38.700
the film, helping spur Disney to create a
slew of live action remakes in the decade

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.700
that followed.

00:03:40.089 --> 00:03:45.290
After a divisive fan reaction to the second
of Disney's "Star Wars" sequel trilogy, Rian

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.840
Johnson's "The Last Jedi," J.J.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.650
Abrams was rushed back into the director's
chair for "Star Wars: Episode IX - The Rise

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:51.840
of Skywalker."

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.049
The result was an ambitious but haphazard
attempt to tire together four decades of continuity

00:03:56.049 --> 00:03:58.409
in a way that was satisfying for obsessed
fans.

00:03:58.409 --> 00:04:02.439
And some fans were happy to get any answers
to long-standing questions and resolutions

00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:06.499
to ongoing character arcs, not to mention
some break-neck action.

00:04:06.499 --> 00:04:10.680
Unfortunately, critics were less than enthused,
and largely knocked the film for a messy script,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.059
choppy storytelling, and one too many confusing
plot points.

00:04:14.304 --> 00:04:19.620
In "Despicable Me 3," lovable former super-villain
Gru now works as an agent for the Anti-Villain

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.980
League, tracking down other baddies and thwarting
their evil schemes.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:28.970
When a job goes wrong, Gru is fired from the
AVL, even losing his beloved minions in the process.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.070
But just when he's struggling with what to
do next, he comes face to face with his long

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:36.130
lost twin brother Dru, who wants lessons on
how to be a super-villain.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.440
And it doesn't go great.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.360
"I should have stayed in the boat.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.820
My stomach feels all queasy.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.150
I shouldn't have eaten that pot pie!"

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:50.850
Though a massive hit in theaters, "Despicable
Me 3" split audiences and critics, who felt

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.833
it was a little too much of the same.

00:04:53.279 --> 00:04:58.290
Going into this live-action remake of the
beloved 1994 animated classic "The Lion King,"

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:02.450
many were skeptical that director Jon Favreau
could bring anything new to the table.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:07.150
But the result was a lush visual feast, with
audiences eating up the awe-inspiring CGI

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:11.070
visuals created using innovative and groundbreaking
new virtual filmmaking techniques.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:15.320
Critics, however, were dismissive of what
they considered a soulless, lackluster remake

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.120
of an indelible original.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.230
Even the return of the legendary James Earl
Jones as King Mufasa wasn't enough to elevate

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.230
the final film.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:30.415
"One day, Simba, the sun will set on my time
here and will rise with you as the new king."

00:05:30.415 --> 00:05:34.470
The breakout stars of the "Despicable Me"
franchise, the pint-sized, overall-wearing

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:38.370
yellow beans called Minions got their own
movie in the wake of "Despicable Me 2."

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:42.360
A prequel to the first "Despicable Me," the
"Minions" movie gives audiences the secret

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.150
origin of the little pill-shaped people, as
we follow their origins from single-celled

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.560
organisms all the way up to them meeting the
super-villain Gru.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.890
Taking the Minions out of "Despicable Me"
and putting them into their own mini-franchise

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:56.440
could have gone terribly wrong, but with a
cast of impeccable voice actors including

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:59.760
Sandra Bullock and John Hamm, it worked surprisingly
well.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.220
After the blockbuster success of other live-action
remakes, Disney looked to their 1992 film

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.550
"Aladdin" for their next big hit.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:11.260
Before the 2019 live action version even arrived,
though, it was mired in controversy over the

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.500
way star Will Smith looked when animated as
a CGI-enhanced blue genie.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:19.600
But once "Aladdin" landed in theaters, audiences
turned out in droves to see the sprawling

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.840
fantasy epic.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:25.070
Fans gave the young cast high marks for infusing
their characters with heart and earnestness,

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:30.490
but critics panned the film, once again questioning
what the point of these live action remakes was.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:36.630
"Aquaman," released in 2018, and opens with
the origin of DC's famous sea-faring superhero.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:40.870
The son of a lighthouse captain and a stranded
woman from Atlantis, young Arthur Curry is

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:45.240
left to be raised on land, ultimately wanting
no part of his watery legacy.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.510
But when a villain threatens war with the
surface world, Curry must finally confront

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.530
his destiny in order to stop them.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:55.100
Led by Jason Momoa, Nicole Kidman, and Willem
DaFoe, the all-star cast gave the film major

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.870
acting talent to go with a pumped up action
spectacle from director James Wan.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.915
Brains, however, could be safely shut off
for the duration of the run time.

00:07:02.915 --> 00:07:04.750
"Pinocchio.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.531
You risked our lives based on something you
read in a children's book?"

00:07:07.531 --> 00:07:10.401
"Wait, it's a book?!"

00:07:10.579 --> 00:07:14.520
The eighth film in the long-running "Fast
and the Furious" series, "The Fate of the

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:19.010
Furious" reunited stars Vin Diesel and Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson in a battle with newcomer

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:21.340
Charlize Theron as the villain Cipher.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:25.860
In this installment of the seemingly never-ending
franchise, Dom Toretto's retirement is upended

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.420
when he's blackmailed into working for the
baddies.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:32.260
The old crew must band together to discover
why Toretto has seemingly turned villain.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:36.960
With some shocking twists and new revelations,
"Fate of the Furious" continued upping the

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.143
ante, with even bigger and bolder action sequences
than ever before.

00:07:40.273 --> 00:07:42.760
Based on the original book by J.R.R.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:46.330
Tolkien, "The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey"
expands greatly on the story.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.512
We meet a homebody hobbit named Bilbo as he
is recruited by Gandalf on a quest to help

00:07:50.512 --> 00:07:53.220
a group of determined dwarves to find a lost
treasure.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:58.070
Along the way, he picks up a little gold ring
that will one day change the fate of all Middle Earth.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:01.920
With Peter Jackson back at the helm, "An Unexpected
Journey" is full of delightful adventure.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:07.090
Overfull, in fact: it's also bloated and indulgent,
leading to a flabby viewing experience that

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.201
turned off fans and critics alike.

00:08:09.201 --> 00:08:15.480
The 2017 live-action remake of the 1991 adaptation
of the 18th century French fairy tale "Beauty

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:19.400
and the Beast" brought the fantasy, starring
"Harry Potter's" Emma Watson and Luke Evans

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.400
of "The Hobbit."

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:24.240
And it tells the same story you go in expecting
to see: Belle's father is taken prisoner by

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.560
a beast, she exchanges places with him, and
unexpected love ensues.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.380
Once again, Disney pulled out all the stops,
loading the film up on luscious eye candy

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:37.530
and top-rate cinematography that dazzled moviegoers,
earning it impressive reviews to go with a

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:39.355
wave of comforting nostalgia.

00:08:39.355 --> 00:08:44.300
It's not often that a sequel can reach the
height of its predecessor, but "Frozen II"

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:48.990
broke the mold, releasing in 2019 to rave
reviews, and ultimately becoming nearly as

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:51.480
beloved as 2013's original "Frozen."

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:56.529
"Frozen II" is another frosty musical tale
that reveals the secret origin of Elsa's powers,

00:08:56.529 --> 00:08:58.790
and the truth behind the death of her parents.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:03.580
Funny, romantic, bittersweet, the film mixes
every emotion with gorgeous 3D animation,

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:08.460
while somehow telling a more nuanced and complex
drama than the first without feeling weighed

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.690
down or over-stuffed with story.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:15.000
It's a testament to Disney's finest storytellers
that they were able to recapture the magic

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.000
of "Frozen."

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.120
Robert Downey Jr. returned in 2013's "Iron
Man 3" as Tony Stark, now dealing with the

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.010
traumatic after effects of the alien invasion
shown in 2012's "Avengers."

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:29.120
But he also has to deal with a new threat
in the form of a notorious global criminal

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:33.770
kingpin called the Mandarin, who turns out
to not exactly be what he seems.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:34.770
"Killian."

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:35.770
"He created you?"

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.400
"He created me."

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.730
"Custom made terror threat?"

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:40.730
"Yes!"

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:45.050
With some of the best "Iron Man" action to
date, the excitement and drama was all there,

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:48.680
with some added heart and depth thanks to
writer/director Shane Black.

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:53.200
Still, the surprising twist regarding the
Mandarin's true nature riled a lot of fans,

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.630
leaving many with decidedly mixed feelings.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:01.190
After the overwhelming success of 2015's "Star
Wars: Episode VII – The Force Awakens,"

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:04.840
Disney turned the keys of the franchise over
to "Looper" director Rian Johnson for the

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:05.840
sequel.

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:08.700
He succeeded in taking the franchise in a
bold new direction with "Star Wars: Episode

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.190
VIII - The Last Jedi."

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:14.380
For many viewers, though, it was the wrong
direction, as Rey discovers that the legendary

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:17.890
Luke Skywalker has given up and become a mopey
cynic.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:21.860
Add in the slowest chase scene in sci-fi history
and a general disregard for everything that

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:25.320
happened in the previous film and you end
up with a movie that was appreciated more

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:27.080
by critics than fans.

00:10:33.869 --> 00:10:39.760
2012's "Avengers" was a massive success, so
for the 2015 sequel "Avengers: Age of Ultron,"

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:42.880
Marvel brought back everyone, including director
Joss Whedon.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:46.730
And then they stuffed it full of even more
characters, introducing the Vision, Quicksilver,

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:50.450
and Scarlet Witch to help battle the new threat
of the murderous robot Ultron.

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:55.450
While some fans praised the action and character
moments in the film, others felt "Age of Ultron"

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:59.460
was a bit bogged down by excessive world-building
at the expense of the story.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:03.404
The world it built, though, would help take
the MCU to undreamt heights.

00:11:03.404 --> 00:11:08.010
Not many franchises make it to seven films,
but the truly amazing thing about "Furious

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:12.320
7" is that it nearly doubled the box office
of "Fast and Furious 6," turning the popular

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.700
series into an absolute unit.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:18.740
In the film, Dom Toretto and his crew are
confronted by Jason Statham's Deckard Shaw,

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:22.360
the vengeance seeking brother of "Fast &amp; Furious
6" villain Owen Shaw.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:26.760
The movie was also the final entry for series
star Paul Walker, who was tragically killed

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:29.840
in an unrelated car accident while the film
was in production.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:33.950
Thanks to the cooperation of his family and
a little CGI magic, producers were able to

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.770
complete his performance and give the actor
a touching send-off that proved an emotional

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.128
moment for fans.

00:11:39.805 --> 00:11:43.920
2003's "Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse
of the Black Pearl" proved audiences would

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.860
turn out for a movie based on a Disney theme
park ride - and the 2006 sequel "Dead Man's

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:53.899
Chest" proved audiences couldn't get enough
of Johnny Depp's antics as Captain Jack Sparrow.

00:11:53.899 --> 00:11:57.970
In this one, Will is ordered to help find
Jack and in turn the fabled Dead Man's Chest,

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:01.880
at the request of the corrupt Lord Beckett,
all while fighting off the legendary Davy

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.940
Jones and his mystical pirate ship the Flying
Dutchman.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:08.310
So big it couldn't get out of its own way,
"Dead Man's Chest" set the franchise on a

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.288
course for the many hits that followed.

00:12:10.561 --> 00:12:16.050
In 2016, "Star Wars" went where it had never
gone before, releasing a standalone live-action

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.490
theatrical film set outside of the main saga.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:23.060
"Rogue One: A Star Wars Story" told the story
of how the Rebellion in "A New Hope" got the

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:27.760
Death Star plans to begin with, with recruits
Jyn Erso and Cassian Andor leading a suicide

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.150
mission to set the stage for the fall of the
Empire.

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:34.220
A darker, grittier take on the franchise,
"Rogue One" was celebrated for it's gritter

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:39.000
take on the mythos, and has been lauded by
some hardcore fans as the best of the recent

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.311
"Star Wars" films.

00:12:40.585 --> 00:12:46.000
Released in 2009, the sci-fi adventure "Avatar"
left viewers' jaws on the floor with its immersive

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.290
vision of a far-off alien world.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:52.060
The film is centered on a race of blue-skinned
natives called the Na'vi, as their home is

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:56.149
invaded by greedy corporate mercenaries who
want to steal their resources.

00:12:56.149 --> 00:13:00.810
Filmed using a new, groundbreaking 3D technology,
"Avatar" proved a moviegoing experience unlike

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:05.080
any other, driving fans into theaters in numbers
nobody had ever thought possible.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:08.770
More than a decade later, it's still the top
grossing film of all time.

00:13:09.073 --> 00:13:13.020
The third in director Christopher Nolan's
trilogy, "The Dark Knight Rises" finished

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:17.570
off what many consider to be the greatest
comic book movie series ever produced.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:21.790
Set almost a decade after the previous film,
"Rises" finds Bruce Wayne retired when a new

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:25.100
and more insidious villain called Bane shows
up on the scene.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:28.710
When Bane's plot to destroy Gotham proves
too much for him, he's forced to sacrifice

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.160
everything to save the city.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.130
While for many "The Dark Knight Rises" could
never live up to "The Dark Knight," it still

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:39.020
remained a satisfying and action-packed conclusion
to the three-film saga, neatly tying the whole

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.250
story together.

00:13:40.409 --> 00:13:47.070
The 2019 sci-fi superhero actioner "Captain
Marvel" was the first MCU film with a woman lead.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:51.230
The film is set in the 1990s, when a valiant
space ranger crash lands on Earth and discovers

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:53.600
she's actually a human woman named Carol Danvers.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:58.130
With the help of a younger Nick Fury, Danvers
must recover her lost memories and uncover

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:01.930
the truth behind the conflict between two
warring alien races.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:06.620
Fans' expectations for the film were so high
that they proved impossible to meet, but "Captain

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:11.459
Marvel" remains a solid entry in the MCU,
and better than it’s often given credit for.

00:14:11.762 --> 00:14:16.700
After the original "Jurassic Park" trilogy
petered out in 2001, it would be 14 years

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:19.550
before "Jurassic World" rebooted the franchise.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:24.330
The 2015 tentpole brought in new stars Chris
Pratt and Bryce Dallas-Howard for a story

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:29.130
about, you guessed it, dinosaurs running rampant
through a tropical island theme park.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:32.760
Only this time, the park is filled with thousands
of tourists for maximum carnage.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:37.080
Debuting with good reviews from both critics
and audiences, "Jurassic World" was lauded

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.820
for its successful mix of modern thrills and
classic "Jurassic Park" storytelling, ultimately

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:43.779
leading to two sequels of its own.

00:14:44.168 --> 00:14:49.640
The first film to ever earn a billion dollars
at the box office, 1997's "Titanic" featured

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:54.149
Leonardo DiCaprio and Kate Winslet as star-crossed
lovers Jack and Rose.

00:14:54.149 --> 00:14:58.470
The poor Jack and the rich Rose find true
love just as the doomed ship famously strikes

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:02.250
an iceberg and pulls most of the film's all-star
cast straight to the bottom.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.250
"Jack!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.890
This is where we first met!"

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:10.250
A tale of love, lust, betrayal, and revenge
set against the backdrop of one of history's

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:13.720
greatest ocean disasters, the film has something
for everyone.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.670
It's no wonder it has remained a beloved classic
for a quarter of a century.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:23.209
Director Todd Phillips turned 2019's "The
Joker" into a gritty and grounded psychological

00:15:23.209 --> 00:15:26.779
drama, and an incisive and surprising takedown
of modern life.

00:15:26.779 --> 00:15:30.900
Touching on such weighty issues as the mental
health system and wealth inequality, star

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:35.810
Joaquin Phoenix turned the clown-faced super-villain
into a deeply troubled soul who resorts to

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.140
violence when society turns its back on him.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:42.040
The results struck a chord with audiences,
who flocked to see the timely film despite

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:45.019
few action scenes and almost no big special
effects.

00:15:45.019 --> 00:15:50.040
Unsurprisingly, a sequel was announced in
2022 and is already in the works.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:54.970
The 2019 blockbuster "Spider-Man: Far From
Home" didn't just build on the legacy of the

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:59.290
previous six "Spider-Man" films, it also provided
the first follow up to the cataclysmic events

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.630
of the MCU-defining "Avengers: Endgame."

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:05.810
The story, about Peter dealing with grief
after the loss of mentor Tony Stark and a

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:10.130
surprising betrayal by new mentor Mysterio,
allowed fans to process their own feelings

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.380
of grief over the death of Iron Man.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:16.611
Mixing coming-of-age teen drama with high
stakes superhero action, "Far From Home" showed

00:16:16.611 --> 00:16:21.273
that the MCU was now centered around a new
figure - and Spider-Man was up to the task.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:26.670
Based on the series of hit young adult fantasy
novels, 2001's "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.620
Stone" introduces audiences to a young orphaned
boy sent to attend Hogwarts School of Witchcraft

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.620
and Wizardry.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:36.589
There he meets new friends who help him discover
the truth when a terrible evil begins threatening

00:16:36.589 --> 00:16:37.589
him and the school.

00:16:37.589 --> 00:16:40.320
"We know about the sorcerer's stone.”

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.660
“Oh."

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:46.899
While the film wasn't as refined or slick
as its successors would be, it drew audiences

00:16:46.899 --> 00:16:51.720
of all ages with its fantasy thrills, family
friendly adventure, and magical mystery, and

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:57.850
turned unknown child actors Daniel Radcliffe,
Emma Watson and Rupert Grint into international stars.

00:16:58.066 --> 00:17:03.830
Another blockbuster from the MCU, 2016's "Captain
America: Civil War" saw the Avengers dealing

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.220
with the aftermath of a mission gone wrong.

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:09.959
When Cap's old sidekick Bucky — now the
Winter Soldier — is accused of killing the

00:17:09.959 --> 00:17:15.699
Wakandan King, our heroes are forced to choose
just whose side they’re on, Cap's or Iron Man's.

00:17:15.699 --> 00:17:19.299
In addition to bringing back old favorites,
the film introduced two big new players for

00:17:19.299 --> 00:17:20.520
the first time.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:24.790
Chadwick Boseman makes his first appearance
as the Black Panther, while Marvel also introduced

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.000
Spider-Man into the MCU.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:32.889
Between the big superhero debuts, the over-the-top
hero-on-hero action, this one was a crowd pleaser.

00:17:32.889 --> 00:17:38.059
Based on the novel by author Michael Crichton,
1993's "Jurassic Park" was quickly optioned

00:17:38.059 --> 00:17:41.630
for a big budget feature film by none other
than Steven Spielberg.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:45.750
He ditched the book's hard science in favor
of an awe-inspiring adventure, with groundbreaking

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.820
special effects that made dinosaurs more real
than ever before.

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:52.679
"Your scientists were so preoccupied with
whether or not they could, they didn't stop

00:17:52.679 --> 00:17:53.809
to think if they should."

00:17:53.809 --> 00:17:58.100
When dinosaurs are cloned, hero scientists
Sam Neill, Laura Dern, and Jeff Goldblum have

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:59.530
to stop them from running amok.

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:04.790
One of the most thrilling and unexpected big
screen joyrides in movie history on its release,

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:09.100
audiences and critics were in awe of the movie
billed as "65 million years in the making."

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:11.600
They could do it, and it turned out they should.

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:17.140
In an unparalleled and monumental undertaking,
the fledgling Marvel Studios set out to craft

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:19.740
the first ever true cinematic universe.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:23.580
After the films "Iron Man," "The Incredible
Hulk," "Captain America" and "Thor" introduced

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:28.070
the individual heroes, 2012's "The Avengers"
brought them all together in a way never seen

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:29.600
in movies before.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:30.730
The story?

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:33.320
Stop Loki and his alien army from conquering
Earth.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:37.770
A sharply written, slickly executed action
blockbuster, not a moment is wasted in the

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:42.440
superhero adventure, which thrilled audiences
and set the stage for a decade of box office

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:43.835
dominance by Marvel.

00:18:43.835 --> 00:18:49.040
It all came to this: 2021's "Spider-Man: No
Way Home" brought back characters from all

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:53.679
seven previous Sony and Marvel Spider-Man
films, as the Spider-Men of three universes

00:18:53.679 --> 00:18:58.000
banded together to try and save the MCU's
Peter Parker from his own mistakes.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.760
Fans thrilled to see Tobey Maguire and Andrew
Garfield stand shoulder to shoulder with Tom

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:06.020
Holland as they fought a menagerie of villains
from all three realities.

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.550
With enough Easter eggs and guest stars to
force fans into theaters despite a global

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:14.000
pandemic, "No Way Home" proved one of the
biggest crowd-pleasers Marvel has ever produced.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:20.240
Loosely inspired by Hans Christian Andersen's
"The Snow Queen," 2013's "Frozen" centers

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:24.880
on Elsa, who fears her own icy supernatural
powers, and has grown estranged from her younger

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:26.410
sister Anna as a result.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:30.790
But when Elsa unwittingly unleashes her power
and covers the kingdom in an icy winter, Anna

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.760
must rekindle their relationship to save everyone.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:39.120
With memorable musical numbers and a timeless
story of family, "Frozen" became an instant classic.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:42.990
Crossing age and gender lines, it was beloved
by audiences of all stripes, helping it become

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.910
an unexpected billion dollar hit.

00:19:45.126 --> 00:19:50.470
2003's "Finding Nemo" was a massive blockbuster
and an instant family classic.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:55.200
But it would be more than a decade before
Pixar followed up with 2016's "Finding Dory,"

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:58.980
which follows Nemo's forgetful friend Dory
as she sets out to regain her memory and find

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.690
her long lost parents.

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:04.540
And along the way, she inevitably meets a
host of new animated undersea buddies.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:08.950
"Finding Dory" was the rare sequel to be not
only a bigger earner than its predecessor,

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:14.538
but an equally crowd-pleasing film, as fans
and critics alike praised it for its heartwarming story.

00:20:14.538 --> 00:20:19.520
2004's "The Incredibles" was one of Pixar's
most beloved films, so it's no surprise that

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:23.910
fans turned out in droves for the 2018 sequel
"The Incredibles 2."

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:29.100
After the fallout from the first film's climactic
battle, the government shuts down their superhero program.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:33.080
But when a wealthy tycoon offers Mr. Incredible
and Elastigirl the chance to become heroes

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:38.960
again, they jump at the chance, only for Elastigirl
to uncover a sinister plot to end all superheroes for good.

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:43.090
With loads of superhero action, delightful
comedy and classic Pixar heart, "Incredibles

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:45.669
2" was a hit in every sense of the word.

00:20:45.669 --> 00:20:50.580
For a full decade, audiences watched Harry
Potter, Hermione Granger, and Ron Weasley

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:55.290
grow up on screen as they fought to stop the
return of the Wizarding World's greatest villain,

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:56.320
Lord Voldemort.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:21:00.910
It all culminated in 2011's "Harry Potter
and the Deathly Hallows, Part 2," as the eighth

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:06.010
and final film in the series saw our heroes
take on Voldemort's army in the Battle of Hogwarts.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.810
"Deathly Hallows, Part II" was not only the
highest grossing film in the franchise, it

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:15.120
also was the most critically acclaimed, earning
three Academy Award nominations and a 96%

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.220
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:18.583
They truly saved the best for last.

00:21:18.583 --> 00:21:23.730
After Disney bought the rights to "Star Wars"
in 2012, it was inevitable that new movies

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:24.730
were coming.

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:29.280
The first was 2015's "Star Wars: Episode VII
- The Force Awakens," which brought back original

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:33.410
characters Han, Leia and Luke and paired them
with a new generation of heroes in the form

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.660
of Rey, Finn, and Poe.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:38.840
While it was knocked for being something of
a rehash, fans loved the familiar, and critics

00:21:38.840 --> 00:21:42.692
praised the picture for re-energizing the
franchise with a promising new story.

00:21:47.496 --> 00:21:48.686
"No!"

00:21:50.729 --> 00:21:55.670
Set in a world of anthropomorphic talking
animals, 2016's animated smash "Zootopia"

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:59.809
features Judy Hopps, an upbeat bunny who enlists
in the local police force.

00:21:59.809 --> 00:22:04.540
Through a series of mishaps, she winds up
stuck with Nick Wilde, a jaded fox con artist

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:06.660
who wants anything but to be paired with Hopps.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:10.490
They soon uncover a major conspiracy that
threatens the city, and must work together

00:22:10.490 --> 00:22:12.100
to get to the truth.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:16.280
Mixing elements from the best buddy cop comedies
with the charms of the best animated family

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:19.914
films, "Zootopia" ultimately won the Academy
Award for best animated film.

00:22:19.914 --> 00:22:24.740
Combining every major Marvel franchise, with
heroes from "The Avengers," "The Guardians

00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:29.880
of the Galaxy," and the recently incorporated
"Spider-Man," 2018's "Avengers: Infinity War"

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:33.960
saw Thanos arrive on Earth to complete his
collection of Infinity Stones, the powerful

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:38.450
ancient relics that will give him the power
to wipe out half of all life in the universe.

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:42.240
An edge-of-your-seat thrill ride from start
to finish, the movie managed to mix dozens

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.620
of heroes and villains together in a story
with a vast canvas.

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:49.160
It satisfied fans of every character, and
delivered something bolder and bigger than

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:54.070
anyone imagined, subverting expectations with
a twist ending that left audiences gasping

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:55.970
in disbelief.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:59.510
"I'm sorry!”

00:23:03.050 --> 00:23:08.160
After 50 years and 23 films, 2012's "Skyfall"
marked the first James Bond movie to crack

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:09.880
the billion dollar mark.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:14.840
In the darkest installment yet, a critical
mission goes wrong and MI6 is compromised.

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:18.730
Daniel Craig's Bond is the only agent left
that can be trusted, and is tasked with tracking

00:23:18.730 --> 00:23:23.150
down and stopping a madman named Silva, an
insidious threat from M's past who has come

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:24.220
back for revenge.

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:28.530
Buoyed by newcomers like Ralph Fiennes, the
film was a tight, gripping spy thriller of

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:33.953
the highest caliber, and many fans and critics
still consider it the high point of modern Bond films.

00:23:34.083 --> 00:23:39.840
Released in 2019, "Toy Story 4" was an unexpected
sequel, as the beloved franchise was seemingly

00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:40.840
over for good.

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:42.160
Luckily, it wasn't.

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:46.350
While on a road trip with their new owner,
Woody is reunited with his old flame Bo Peep,

00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:48.400
who tries to get him to run away with her.

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:52.460
Now Woody must decide whether he wants a future
with a child as he has always believed was

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:55.570
intended, or the freedom of a new life as
a rogue toy.

00:23:55.570 --> 00:23:59.150
Once again, Pixar knocked it out of the park
with fans and critics alike.

00:23:59.150 --> 00:24:02.660
Now the only question is whether there will
ever be a "Toy Story 5."

00:24:02.934 --> 00:24:08.429
Combining lush, vibrant, and expressive animation
with a number of iconic new songs and powerful

00:24:08.429 --> 00:24:12.580
storytelling, 1994's "The Lion King" was a
worldwide sensation.

00:24:12.580 --> 00:24:17.060
In this animated Shakespearean tragedy, young
cub prince Simba runs in fear after his uncle

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:19.820
Scar murders his father, King Mufasa.

00:24:19.820 --> 00:24:23.660
But when Simba's childhood friend Nala finds
him, he is urged to return to the pride and

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:25.980
save his former home from the cruelty of his
uncle.

00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:30.390
One of the most acclaimed and beloved films
of all time, "The Lion King" has enjoyed multiple

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.816
re-releases over the years to help it cross
the billion dollar mark.

00:24:33.816 --> 00:24:39.429
Marvel Comics' first Black superhero debuted
in 1966 in the pages of "Fantastic Four,"

00:24:39.429 --> 00:24:44.030
but it would take until 2017 for "Black Panther"
to get his own feature film.

00:24:44.030 --> 00:24:47.610
Expectations were through the roof, but even
the most fervent fans were blown away by director

00:24:47.610 --> 00:24:50.620
Ryan Coogler's vision of afro-futurism.

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:54.510
But it was actor Chadwick Boseman who provided
the heart of this story, which centers around

00:24:54.510 --> 00:24:58.580
a challenge to the ideologies of Wakanda by
T'Challa's cousin Killmonger.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:05.110
Tragically, Boseman passed away in 2020 at
the age of 43, leaving an indelible legacy behind.

00:25:05.110 --> 00:25:07.130
"Wakanda forever!"

00:25:07.130 --> 00:25:12.289
2008's "The Dark Knight" is one of most critically
acclaimed superhero films of all time.

00:25:12.289 --> 00:25:16.340
Heath Ledger stars as the Joker, who sets
out to prove humanity isn't worth saving by

00:25:16.340 --> 00:25:21.169
exposing all the hypocrisy, greed, and selfishness
beneath the surface of Gotham City.

00:25:21.169 --> 00:25:24.840
Directed by Christopher Nolan and starring
Christian Bale as Batman, "The Dark Knight"

00:25:24.840 --> 00:25:26.059
was a tour-de-force.

00:25:26.059 --> 00:25:30.919
Tragically, star Heath Ledger died just months
before release, but he'd get the last laugh

00:25:30.919 --> 00:25:34.404
on his doubters as his performance earned
him a posthumous Oscar.

00:25:34.404 --> 00:25:40.320
36 years after the original "Top Gun" debuted
in theaters, 2022's "Top Gun: Maverick" blew

00:25:40.320 --> 00:25:44.170
audience expectations out of the sky with
the return of Tom Cruise's legendary fight

00:25:44.170 --> 00:25:46.460
pilot Pete "Maverick" Mitchell.

00:25:46.460 --> 00:25:50.120
Called back into service to help train a group
of young recruits for a crucial mission behind

00:25:50.120 --> 00:25:54.120
enemy lines, Maverick gets more than he bargained
for when he learns one of the cadets is the

00:25:54.120 --> 00:25:58.200
son of his old friend Goose, who died in an
accident for which he has long felt responsible.

00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:00.020
"My dad believed in you.

00:26:00.020 --> 00:26:02.580
I'm not gonna make the same mistake."

00:26:02.580 --> 00:26:06.700
Praised by critics, "Top Gun: Maverick" soared
to become one of the best reviewed films of

00:26:06.700 --> 00:26:09.932
the year, and the best of Tom Cruise's long
career.

00:26:09.932 --> 00:26:15.370
The culmination of more than a decade of films,
2019's "Avengers: Endgame" might be the most

00:26:15.370 --> 00:26:20.210
highly anticipated superhero movie ever, coming
a year after "Infinity War" left fans stunned

00:26:20.210 --> 00:26:23.200
by Thanos' victory and the loss of half of
our heroes.

00:26:23.200 --> 00:26:27.840
"Avengers: Endgame" sees the surviving heroes
engage in a desperate time heist to try and

00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:29.520
alter reality itself.

00:26:29.520 --> 00:26:33.870
But Thanos has other plans, only stopped when
Tony Stark sacrifices himself to save the

00:26:33.870 --> 00:26:36.220
entire universe from oblivion.

00:26:36.220 --> 00:26:40.700
Featuring action on a scale never before imagined,
"Endgame" was the ultimate theater experience

00:26:40.700 --> 00:26:42.436
for an entire generation.

00:26:42.436 --> 00:26:48.240
Coming out a decade after "Toy Story 2," 2010's
"Toy Story 3" sees the toys from Andy's room

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:52.731
mistakenly donated to a daycare center, where
the plush monstrosity Lots-o'-Huggin Bear

00:26:52.731 --> 00:26:54.140
rules with terror.

00:26:54.140 --> 00:26:58.880
Woody, Buzz, and the rest must band together
to lead a toy rebellion in order to save themselves

00:26:58.880 --> 00:27:00.590
from certain doom.

00:27:00.590 --> 00:27:04.480
Receiving universal critical acclaim, "Toy
Story 3" served as a perfect conclusion to

00:27:04.480 --> 00:27:07.180
the story of Woody, Buzz, and the gang.

00:27:07.180 --> 00:27:11.340
Of course, another sequel eventually followed
and a fifth may be on the way, but "Toy Story

00:27:11.340 --> 00:27:14.039
3" still remains the best reviewed film in
the series.

00:27:14.486 --> 00:27:18.450
"The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the
King" capped off the epic fantasy film trilogy

00:27:18.450 --> 00:27:21.190
from director Peter Jackson in 2003.

00:27:21.190 --> 00:27:24.830
The final film in the series sees Sam and
Frodo making their final journey to the steps

00:27:24.830 --> 00:27:29.951
of Mount Doom, while Aragorn, Gandalf, and
an army of men confront Sauron's forces in

00:27:29.951 --> 00:27:32.470
a final showdown between the forces of good
and evil.

00:27:32.470 --> 00:27:37.680
A box office smash, "Return of the King" put
a perfect bow on the "Lord of the Rings" film saga.

00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:41.220
Not only is it the highest grossing film in
the series, it also took home the Academy

00:27:41.220 --> 00:27:44.959
Award for Best Picture – the only fantasy
film to ever do so.

00:27:44.959 --> 00:27:47.352
"You bow to no one."

